sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-055-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Figs. 394-400: rhinoceros and allied skulls by coordinate-grid transformation (Osborn) — MorphoEval overall 82.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2), overall 82.7/100 (up from 67.0 in Pass 1). Nine panels digitised from SHA-256-pinned IA crops; primary Hyrachyus (394) -> Aceratherium (395) with 40 matched grid nodes at defaults. TPS applied to the Hyrachyus boundary: Procrustes 0.370 vs identity 0.377 vs affine 0.360; IoU 0.570 (affine 0.587); Pearson r 0.976; chamfer/cs 0.015; shuffled-grid null worse than nominal. Parameter sweep: 36 primary-only settings; 27/27 with >=40 matches beat identity on Procrustes; affine beats TPS throughout those rows. min det D phi_t inside skull 0.259. Secondary 3/6 beat identity. Ceratotherium CV descriptive. Verdict mixed. Overall 82.1/100 (faithfulness 81.1, reproducibility 84.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 530b3b50c; environment: python 3.12, numpy 1.26.4, scipy 1.x (pip, requirements.txt lower bound >=1.7), scikit-image >=0.19, matplotlib >=3.3, Pillow >=8.0, lean 4.35.0 (elan stable). Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 77, Parameter expressivity 79, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 81. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_055_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-055_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 530b3b50c, image/png, 540693 B, 1980×1100 px, artifact_sha256 65d3271d99b1aa5c2c476ae8f90ab25d1dfc51663e05b92ff0b626a382f24254 (sha256 65d3271d99b1aa5c2c476ae8f90ab25d1dfc51663e05b92ff0b626a382f24254), spec_fingerprint 1799c9e22b84705ed0af5fe44b5529c9ffab5f336a64446d6582253a48d2e8c1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1799c9e22b84705ed0af5fe44b5529c9ffab5f336a64446d6582253a48d2e8c1; artifact_sha256: 65d3271d99b1aa5c2c476ae8f90ab25d1dfc51663e05b92ff0b626a382f24254; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ceratotherium_simum_skull_mnhn_1400.jpg=7ed8c3776d2ab62a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p761_leaf0781_figs394-395.jpg=978a7d9039629c42..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p762_leaf0782_fig396.jpg=7a8a134814786620..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p763_leaf0783_figs397-398.jpg=229d3074b7e141bf..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/ongrowthform1917thom_p764_leaf0784_figs399-400.jpg=5dcb998220348ea5..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-055/t1917_055_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=ee9eba19f703221d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-055-on-the-theory-of-transformatio-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Fig. 394 Hyrachyus skull with rectangular Cartesian grid; Fig. 395 Aceratherium in a deformed grid (p. 760-761) | occipital Aceratherium variants related by conformal transformations (Fig. 396, p. 762) | extensions to Titanotherium, tapir, horse, and rabbit by the same method (Figs. 397-400, pp. 763-764) | methodological claim that allied skulls differ by smooth coordinate transformation of a common diagram; reconstructed_in_script: phi as TPS on automatically matched grid peaks; identity, affine, and shuffled-grid controls | IoU, Pearson r, RMSE/cs, chamfer/cs, Procrustes; primary-only parameter sweep; E1 Jacobian check | Ceratotherium photograph bone/matrix mask (descriptive, excluded from verdict statistics); transfer_boundary: automatic NN grid matching still approximates Thompson's hand correspondences | affine beating TPS on Procrustes and IoU means the registered non-affine spline claim is only partially supported for Aceratherium; does_not_claim: that TPS strictly dominates affine on the primary pair (it does not on Procrustes or IoU) | that modern 3D GM datasets validate the rabbit/horse panels (Leporidae cache mismatch) | that Ceratotherium segmentation quantifies the Osborn diagram fit." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [digitisation/specimen-match, pressure P=2.5]: Hand-labelled grid correspondences or independent digitisation of Fig. 394-395 grid ink",
            "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: Independent second assessor from a different provider",
            "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.5]: Resolve affine-vs-TPS ambiguity: Thompson-like sparse anchor grid or literature 2-D landmarks for Osborn skulls",
            "remediation needed: R1 (open): independent second assessor from a different provider — this round is builder-scored",
            "remediation needed: R7: hand-digitise grid line intersections on Figs. 394-395 and compare with automatic peak matching",
            "remediation needed: R8: sparse-anchor or conformal grid matching Thompson's occipital Fig. 396 panels to test whether non-affine phi is required once correspondences are fixed",
            "remediation needed: R9: assemble open 2-D skull landmarks for perissodactyl intermediates to test secondary pairs beyond diagram self-consistency" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.821"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (builder-assessor, single-agent Pass 2; second assessor pending)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://ai.google.dev> .
}

